<Base title="Corrections policy — GovWait" description="How to report a processing-time mismatch and how GovWait investigates, corrects and documents errors." noindex={true}>
  <nav class="crumbs"><a href="/">Home</a> › Corrections</nav>
  <h1>Corrections policy</h1>
  <p class="lede">The official agency wins whenever a GovWait value and its source disagree. Reports of mismatches are investigated against the primary source and append-only history.</p>

  <h2>Report a possible error</h2>
  <p>Email <a href="mailto:contact@govwait.com?subject=Possible%20GovWait%20data%20correction">contact@govwait.com</a> with:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>the exact GovWait URL;</li>
    <li>the official government URL;</li>
    <li>the value and date you observed; and</li>
    <li>a short description of the mismatch.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>Do not send an application number, passport, decision letter or other personal case material.</p>

  <h2>How corrections work</h2>
  <ol>
    <li>We reproduce the issue against the current official source.</li>
    <li>We check the stored raw observation, parser output and validation record.</li>
    <li>If GovWait is wrong, publication is blocked until the parser or page is corrected and the full validation suite passes.</li>
    <li>A genuine official change is added as a new dated observation. Prior official observations are not silently rewritten.</li>
  </ol>
  <p>Spelling, explanation or accessibility errors in GovWait’s own text are corrected directly, with the page’s modified date updated when the change is material.</p>
</Base>
